---
title: ProximaDB - Partition Lease State Machine (CockroachDB-style per-range leaseholder)
---
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Unheld: No existing lease

    state "LEASE LIFECYCLE" as Lifecycle {
        Unheld --> Acquiring: acquire() called\n(read current lease body)

        Acquiring --> Held: commit_fenced() succeeds\n(new gen = prior_gen + 1\nCAS put_if_absent on successor slot)
        Acquiring --> Unheld: CAS fails (another pod won)\n→ LeaseOutcome::Held(holder_info)

        Held --> Renewing: renewal timer fires\n(typically TTL/3)
        Renewing --> Held: re-commit succeeds\n(same generation, fresh expiry)
        Renewing --> Fenced: CAS rejected\n(higher-gen lease exists)

        Held --> Expired: expiry_ms elapsed\n(no renewal in time)
        Expired --> Unheld: lease body marked stale

        Fenced --> [*]: step down, release locks\n→ LeaseOutcome::Fenced
    }

    state "WRITE FENCING" as Fencing {
        state "Writer submits with generation G" as Submit
        state "Compare G vs current lease gen" as Compare
        state "Write allowed" as Allowed
        state "Write rejected (stale writer)" as Rejected

        Submit --> Compare
        Compare --> Allowed: G >= current_gen
        Compare --> Rejected: G < current_gen\n(fenced — newer pod owns lease)
    }

    state "TAKEOVER" as Takeover {
        state "Pod A holds lease (gen=3)" as HoldA
        state "Pod B reads lease, sees expired" as ReadB
        state "Pod B commits gen=4" as CommitB
        state "Pod A tries renew gen=3 → fenced" as FenceA

        HoldA --> ReadB: expiry elapsed
        ReadB --> CommitB: CAS succeeds
        CommitB --> FenceA: Pod A renewal rejected
    }

    state "RESOURCE TYPE DISPATCH" as Dispatch {
        state "PartitionLeaseManager" as PLM
        state "Collection strategy" as CollStrat
        state "Table strategy" as TableStrat
        state "Graph strategy" as GraphStrat
        state "Document strategy" as DocStrat
        state "Model strategy" as ModelStrat

        PLM --> CollStrat: ResourceType::Collection
        PLM --> TableStrat: ResourceType::Table | Schema
        PLM --> GraphStrat: ResourceType::Graph | GraphNode | GraphEdge
        PLM --> DocStrat: ResourceType::Document | Doc
        PLM --> ModelStrat: ResourceType::Model | ModelVersion | Experiment | FeatureSet
    }

    note right of Held
        Manifest path:
        {prefix}/{tenant}/{collection}/_manifests/
        Lease body committed via ManifestCommitter::commit_fenced()
        Generation header provides correctness fence
        Clocks passed explicitly (now_ms) for determinism
    end note

    note right of Fencing
        Object-store fence = correctness authority
        Partition lease = latency optimization
        No two pods can hold same partition simultaneously
    end note
